# Architecture Rules

Prefer complete vertical slices:

UI → query/data layer → API contract → controller → application/service → repository/integration
→ database/external service → response DTO → frontend.

Keep domain boundaries explicit.

Do not create microservices merely because the domain has multiple modules. The planned backend
starts as a modular NestJS application and may extract telehealth, notifications/workers,
billing/claims workers or audit/event processing only when justified.

Frontend responsibilities:

- presentation and interaction;
- local UI state;
- server-state consumption through TanStack Query;
- form state through React Hook Form;
- validation through shared schemas where appropriate;
- API calls through a dedicated API/data layer.

Backend responsibilities:

- authentication;
- authorization;
- tenant enforcement;
- validation;
- business rules;
- persistence;
- integrations;
- audit events.

Never move security-sensitive authorization decisions into the frontend only.
